# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

Every file in #5289's table gets written one record per line by a single layout function: `crates/tools/src/json_layout.rs`'s `layout`, with a JavaScript copy in `apps/web/scripts/json-layout.mjs`. Every writer of those files uses it. A new `cargo jackioh format-json` command rewrites the tree once. `format-json --check`, run from `crates/tools/tests/acceptance.rs`, fails on any file that is not already in this layout.

The contents stay the same, because the layout only moves white space outside strings. Ruling R5289000 records the format and its one effect on the history: a win-rate table, card list or records table shipped before this change keeps its `shipped.json` blob, which is the hash of the old two-space form.

